Back optimal images on imported host memory with a linear Metal texture.

KosmicKrisp places an optimal (tiled) image only in a MTLHeap, and asserts in
kk_image_plane_bind that memory has one. Memory imported through
VK_EXT_external_memory_host is a plain MTLBuffer with no heap, and Metal cannot
place a tiled texture on a buffer -- only a linear one. MoltenVK handled this by
backing such textures linearly; KosmicKrisp did not, so an optimal image bound
to imported host memory aborted.

This matters under venus (virglrenderer): venus gives the guest memory by
importing a host pointer, and this device exposes a single host-visible memory
type, so every guest allocation is imported host memory with no heap. Without
this, no optimal image can bind, and the first one a guest creates aborts the
renderer -- which is what vk_smoke hit on the first clear-image.

The fix converts the plane to a linear layout when the memory has no heap, and
takes the existing buffer-backed texture path. It is invisible to the guest: an
optimal image has an opaque layout the guest may not inspect, so a linear
backing is a valid choice. It covers the 2D single-level case a buffer-backed
Metal texture and calc_linear both require, which is what a shared render target
or a transfer image is; a mip/array/3D image on imported memory is not handled
and would still assert, but venus does not put those on host-visible memory.

Reported upstream territory -- KosmicKrisp is alpha and this is MoltenVK parity
it has not reached yet.

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
index de27a6d..d328a06 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
@@ -852,6 +852,20 @@ kk_image_plane_bind(struct kk_device *dev, struct kk_image *image,
                                &plane_align_B);
    *offset_B = align64(*offset_B, plane_align_B);
 
+   /* Memory with no Metal heap is imported host memory (VK_EXT_external_memory_host),
+    * which is a plain MTLBuffer. Metal cannot place an optimal (tiled) texture on
+    * a buffer, only a linear one, so an optimal image bound here is backed
+    * linearly instead -- the same thing MoltenVK does. The guest never inspects
+    * an optimal image's opaque layout, so a linear backing is invisible to it;
+    * it only works for a 2D single-level image, which is what calc_linear and a
+    * buffer-backed Metal texture both require, and what a shared render target is.
+    * Every venus allocation lands here because this device exposes one
+    * host-visible memory type, so without this no optimal image could bind. */
+   if (!mem->bo->mtl_handle && !plane->layout.linear) {
+      plane->layout.linear = true;
+      kk_image_layout_calc_linear(dev, &plane->layout);
+   }
+
    assert(plane->layout.linear || mem->bo->mtl_handle);
 
    /* Linear textures in Metal need to be allocated through a buffer... */
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_layout.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_layout.c
index f91bfa8..bf87d56 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_layout.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_layout.c
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ kk_image_layout_can_optimize(const struct kk_physical_device *pdev,
    return true;
 }
 
-static void
+void
 kk_image_layout_calc_linear(const struct kk_device *dev,
                             struct kk_image_layout *layout)
 {
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_layout.h b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_layout.h
index 0e2a054..17c044d 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_layout.h
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_layout.h
@@ -221,4 +221,10 @@ void kk_image_layout_init(const struct kk_device *dev,
                           const uint8_t width_scale, const uint8_t height_scale,
                           struct kk_image_layout *layout);
 
+/* Recompute a layout as linear (2D, single level). Used when an image is bound
+ * to memory with no Metal heap -- imported host memory -- where an optimal
+ * texture cannot be placed and a buffer-backed linear one is the only option. */
+void kk_image_layout_calc_linear(const struct kk_device *dev,
+                                 struct kk_image_layout *layout);
+
 #endif /* KK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_H */
